  "description": "The G13 shows that the GEOLUTION geometry works on trail bikes with 29-inch tires too. Whether you go for a multi-day alpine tour or only for a short, fast time at your local trail, the G13 makes both up and down quicker. Steep climbing with “old school” geometry bikes tends to lift the front wheel, not so with the G13. Due to the seat tube angle and the central seating position your front wheel will stay on the ground and the climb will be clean and controlled.\n\nAll “G” models have been completely redesigned including a new swingarm and adjustable dropouts which are lighter and stiffer. Likewise, the suspension response has been fine tuned with the use of quadruple sealed ball bearings. Sealed for the applause of the people taking the ION-G13 on wet and muddy winter rides. The proven Nicolai shock lever has been pushed through many FEM strength calculations in order to reduce the weight while keeping the same rigidity. Although our 5-axis CNC machine now runs a little longer, as a reward it’s lighter.",
